  "concept_layer": {
    "purpose": "The single valid bridge between the document branch and the structured branch. Both sides map into one shared concept vocabulary and are joined there.",
    "JOIN_RULE": "Join the two branches on the CONCEPT NAME, never on the C01-C29 category code. The codes conflict across branches (structured C11=tickets vs document C16=Complaints; structured C18=porting vs document C06=Number Portability; structured C05=payments vs document C05=SIM Card Services). A code join succeeds and is silently wrong.",
    "vocabulary_source": "The distinct shared_domain_concept values of structured_document_crosswalk. No parallel names are invented: a concept is either already in that column or it does not exist.",
    "concept_count": 23,
    "concepts": [
      "Billing & Invoices",
      "Broadband & FTTH Services",
      "Complaints & Grievances",
      "Customer Account",
      "Device Compatibility",
